A||N||9||Formula88||Got Beer||||10||
Z||000000||Formula88||02-20-2001||08:52 PM||||So, people, anyone here a beer aficianado, like myself?  Not just any type of beer, but good beer.  Have you heard of a little place down in Manteo, NC called The Weeping Radish? Some of the best beer I've ever had.  So, what's your favorite?  On draught, bottle?  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BeerHeaven.jpg"> <BR>This is the motherload of 5L kegs of various flavours of Weeping Radish beer that LZeitgeist & I brought back from the Weeping Radish for the holidays.  Unfiltered and unpasteurized!  God, that was good beer.  ||||reg||10
Z||000001||batboy||02-20-2001||10:07 PM||||And I thought the Foster's oil cans were big. I want a Crying Onion... or was it Weeping Radish! Lots of good micro-brews out now. Hard to pick a favorite. A guy at work makes excellent homemade beer... he even grows his own hopps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||02-20-2001||10:35 PM||||I know what you mean.  So many microbrews, so little liver left....   I've gone to the Southeaster Microbrew Invitational several years.  I've been to tastings of Microbrews from around the world.  The Weeping Radish is the best I've ever found.  Their Black Radish is their darkest, but not as heavy as Guiness - very hoppy flavour.  The Fest is more of a Red-Amber beer closer to a Newcastle or Killians.  Then the Corrolla Gold is the lightest beer, which I was quite surprised to find out I liked (I'm a porter/stout fan myself).  The best yet was an experiment on New Years Eve when we tried to make a Black and Tan out of Black Radish and Fest.  It wouldn't layer for crap, but oh god was it good!  You can sometimes find Weeping Radish beer in the grocery stores, but the bottled can't compete with the fresh from the keg flavour (obviously).  And, no, I'm not on their payroll. I just want to spread the joy of W.R. beer to the world, because it's hard enough for me to find it here in NC!  I want it to be available everywhere beer is sold.  But then, the beer runs to the coast (East bound and down....) are SO much fun!!  Do you know how many 5L kegs you can fit into a Fiero?  LZeitgeist and I are making another run soon.  Twin 88 Formulas blasting to the coast for beer!  Maybe this time I won't get a ticket!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||02-20-2001||10:38 PM||||Oh, yea.  Check out their website: <A HREF="http://www.weepingradish.com" TARGET=_blank>www.weepingradish.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||crzyone||02-21-2001||08:57 AM||||When your done with those kegs you can sell them to Ricers!  Probibly make your money back...  That would probibly add 40HP at least, look at the size of them!<P>I'm leaving now...<P>------------------<BR>86 GT fastback 4 speed<BR>85 sport coupe 5 speed||||reg||1
