Z||000007||Greg Piet||02-21-2001||12:43 PM||||I have had weeping raddish but I wouldnt call it by any means a great beer.  Its a better beer for the price, but I do not see it coming close to Pilser Urqwell, Murphys, or Newcastle.  I must confess I am a Stout drinker more than a Pilsner drinker, so I am biased.<BR>I think when I bought a 12pack(bottles not those funky cans/mini kegs) of the weeping raddish it was cheaper than Budweiser for cost as well.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||02-21-2001||02:37 PM||||Yea, Greg, that's the problem with W/R beer, it's flavour is rather delicate and the filtering and pasteurization does change the character of the beer.  The 5L kegs we got came right out of the tap at the Weeping Radish.  As such, they have to be kept refrigerated at all times.  Can't really do that with regular bottled beer, so the flavour does suffer somewhat.  That's why I'm on a mission to get it on draught in as many places as possible!  Personally, I prefer it to all the beers you mention (yes, I've tried them all), but to each his own.  I do like a hoppy beer.  Another of my favorites is Battlefield Black, by Spring Garden Brewery (I believe).  It's another dark beer with a very hoppy flavour and aroma.||||reg||6
Z||000009||LZeitgeist||02-26-2001||08:51 AM||||Yeah, buddy - we gotta make that run soon. I'm down to 10 litres, and we need to pop one of those when we get your car back together. <P>If you guys have had Weeping Radish in a bottle, you've had the worst representative of the brand (which is actually still not too bad...) - it just does not and can not compare to the stuff fresh out of the vat at the Manteo location. The next best thing is the 5 litre kegs shown above, or the flip-top 1-litre bottles. The difference is that the commercially available six-pack bottles have been filtered and pasturized, and while that's normal for bottled beer, it takes away a lot of the character and signature flavor of the beer. <P>I think I've got a free weekend in mid-March... we gotta make that run! ||||reg||1
